with the holiday shopping season here  online retailers are hoping sales  continue to surge this year a National  Retail Federation estimates sixty-eight  point seven million Americans will shop  online this Cyber Monday and last year  Amazon the biggest online retailer sold  more than a hundred and eighty million  items over the five-day period from  Thanksgiving to Cyber Monday but what  you might not know is that the item you  just bought online could have been  sitting on your local store shelf  moments before you paid for it we went  out on the road to meet the people who  are shopping just to sell and what are  you hoping to find I'm hoping to find  some toys today toy Chris Anderson goes  to great lengths to land a deal logging  40,000 miles a year in his van Anderson  is an Amazon seller practicing retail  arbitrage here's how it works  a seller like Anderson buys an item for  a discounted price in one market like a  store and then sells it for a profit in  another market such as Amazon when  Anderson spots a promising deal he uses  a smartphone app to see just how much  and how often it's selling for online  then he scales up buying it again and  again it all goes into his van and then  to his 200,000 square foot warehouse in  central Pennsylvania once it sells it  goes to an amazon fulfillment center and  then on to the buyer its bargain hunting  on a big scale and anderson pockets the  profit all of this here is about $2,000  worth of soy sauce and i bought it from  a trader in philadelphia and you're  gonna sell it for probably five to ten  thousand dollars yeah that's a lot of  money it is but it's also a lot of work  how far have you gone to find your deals  oh I've driven all the way down to  Florida all the way up to Maine  Massachusetts I've gone all the way out  to Iowa pretty much anywhere I bet you  found some unusual things though  absolutely were the more unusual things  I found was a whole bunch of beer tap  handles I found it  200 of those in a store and they're like  40 50 bucks on eBay and Amazon and I was  buying them for $5.00 and sold them all  real fast people love them so it's the  unusual yeah it's the discontinued the  hard-to-find I'm gonna play a game with  you name that item back scratcher never  sold back scratchers fur coats don't do  fur raincoats  oh I've sold a lot of raincoats nose  clippers I sell a lot of personal care  items mousetraps  I've sold mousetraps good moneymaker not  really  some of these will see a 30 $40 profit  on other ones we'll see you 15 or 20 Wow  arbitrage is nothing new outlets like  Amazon eBay Craigslist Facebook  marketplace and Poshmark have  turbocharged the business this Brady  here I was picking these up for  literally like two three bucks and they  were calling for like 15 16 dollars all  day long that's led to an online  community of sellers who are getting in  on the action they are today including  my crazy Resendez yeah I think we might  have hit a little bit of a jackpot here  he's been selling products online for 15  years when I looked this up on Amazon  the rink is a hundred and nine thousand  and home improvement which isn't bad but  selling it for 43 25 FBA would only pay  out 33 18 and since we have to pay 35  plus tax to buy this that that is a  no-go now easy says he's done five  million dollars in sales on Amazon alone  often spending thousands of dollars on a  single shopping trip to flip all this  merchandise we have so much data  available to us as sellers it's not like  back in the day when you ran a store and  you ordered product you don't know  what's gonna sell well I know what's  selling I know how fast it's selling I  know what it's selling for on average  and so I know how much I can buy there's  no there's not a lot of guesswork  involved in it like  profit minimum to as much as 600 dollars  in profit in there right there 30  minutes later but raizy takes it a step  further his YouTube channel breezy  resells is dedicated to helping novice  sellers stay in the black top clearance  stuff is down low and up high let other  people in on how good you got so what  happened was for the longest time I  didn't tell anybody what I did and I was  super like I thought I was like James  Bond right I was super quiet about it I  always wanted to help people and change  the world and then I was like oh this is  how I'm gonna do it I'm gonna teach  people how to make money online and  they're gonna appreciate that and oddly  enough I actually make more money now  that I share information cuz oh it's  like the universe just keeps giving back  and that's what I'm a fan of kind of a  pay it forward mentality yeah definitely  and it's paying you back they actually  make more money now doing the YouTube  and the social media  then I do actually selling stuff I  didn't really start out helping people I  just started doing it and then what  happened was I would get messages from  people and they'd be like oh you helped  me oh we're in Disneyland with the kids  and it's all because of you you know  people would find me in public and  approach me crying like oh I paid off my  college loan debt because of you and I'm  like oh wow it's something we saw  firsthand on a recent shopping trip with  Reesie  I saw your videos I like how you're  giving people tips  as a site income but while folks like  resi make it look easy there are plenty  of risks involved if this is going to be  your actual way of making a living then  there are hard costs that are wired into  the process so it's not just the  warehouse and it's the time and it's  insurance and it's being able to  actually keep track of what you have  it's not for everybody and I think it's  probably not for most people but that  doesn't keep Chris Anderson from living  a life out on the road this has been the  best job I've ever had  so Anderson's shopping his way from  Pennsylvania to Minnesota during this  big shopping week and while he has that  big van he's part 